            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your 74-year-old male patient, admitted on 02/01/2011 with an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Clinical examination, chest X-ray, arterial blood gas analysis, and pulse oximetry confirmed an acute exacerbation. Blood tests were obtained to exclude infection and monitor inflammatory markers. The patient was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy, resulting in satisfactory clinical improvement. Vital signs were monitored continuously throughout the stay. The patient was discharged in stable condition with adjusted inhaler therapy and is kindly referred back to your care for ongoing COPD management and follow-up. Yours sincerely, Dr. [Treating Physician], Department of Internal Medicine</div>
               </text>
            </section>
